### Normalized scores (1–100)

- **Tool use: 75/100.** Part of GPT-6 generation with tool calling support. Positioned for focused tasks rather than complex agentic work. Capped by absent benchmarks and efficiency-first design.
- **Reasoning: 72/100.** Smallest GPT-6 model; designed for well-defined tasks rather than deep reasoning. Communication quality matches Astra. Capped by efficiency-focused positioning.
- **Context window: 88/100.** 1.05M-token window with 128K output matches GPT-6 family top tier. Capped by absent retrieval benchmarks.
- **Multimodal: 70/100.** Text + image input; text-only output. Same modality as GPT-6 Sol. Capped by vision-only scope.
- **Coding: 70/100.** Suitable for routine coding tasks but not positioned as a coding leader. Capped by absent benchmarks and efficiency-first design.
- **Cost efficiency: 97/100.** $0.10/$0.50 per 1M is among the cheapest frontier-class models. $0.01 cached input is remarkably cheap. Available to free-tier users.
- **Overall Score: 75/100.** Mean of (75 + 72 + 88 + 70 + 70) / 5 = 75.0. Exceptional cost-efficiency in the GPT-6 generation, constrained by efficiency-focused design.

